type: software
title: "CT Spine & Pelvis → 3D Bone Mesh Pipeline"
authors:
  - family-names: Mithani
    given-names: Aditya
    email: mcgillspacemed@gmail.com
date-released: "2026-11-03"
url: "https://github.com/<your-username>/<your-repo>"
repository-code: "https://github.com/<your-username>/<your-repo>"
abstract: >-
  Segments spine and pelvis CT scans from open datasets (CTSpinoPelvic1K, VerSe 2020,
  TotalSegmentator dataset v3), compares automatic segmentation methods against each
  dataset's own published labels, and cleans every segmented bone into a watertight,
  quality-checked finite-element mesh, including a two-material (cortical/trabecular)
  mesh as groundwork for CT-density-derived bone material properties.
keywords:
  - medical imaging
  - CT segmentation
  - finite element mesh
  - spine
  - pelvis
  - biomechanics
